# ── Provider keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# At least ONE of the two must be set, or the server refuses to boot.
#
#   MEESHO_GATEWAY_VK — virtual key for the Meesho bifrost gateway. This single
#                       gateway serves every non-Groq model (GPT-4o, Gemini 2.5,
#                       Claude) over an OpenAI-compatible wire, authenticated with
#                       the x-bf-vk header. Set this to use those models.
#   GROQ_API_KEY      — Groq's own API key. Only needed for the `llama-groq` model,
#                       which is the one model called directly (not via the gateway).
MEESHO_GATEWAY_VK=
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Provider base URLs — override only for a proxy / self-hosted endpoint.
# MEESHO_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=http://llm-gateway.prd.meesho.int/v1
# GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1

# ── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APP_ENV=dev  → permissive (auto-migrate, demo login allowed, relative paths ok).
# APP_ENV=prod → config.Validate() hard-fails the boot on any insecure default
#                (dev JWT secret, missing ALLOWED_ORIGINS, COOKIE_SECURE=false,
#                AUTH_MODE=demo, relative DB_PATH/PRICING_PATH).
# APP_ENV=dev

# ── Server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=8000
# PRICING_PATH=./pricing.json   # absolute path required in prod

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_DRIVER selects the backend; only the matching location var is used.
#   sqlite   → DB_PATH   (a file; absolute path required in prod)
#   postgres → DB_DSN    (e.g. postgres://user:pass@host:5432/llm_platform?sslmode=require)
# Run `go run ./cmd/migrate` (or cmd/bootstrap) to apply the schema; the server
# only auto-migrates in dev.
# DB_DRIVER=sqlite
# DB_PATH=./llm_platform.db
# DB_DSN=

# ── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated frontend origin(s). Required in prod. With the subdomain
# topology this is the Studio origin, e.g. https://studio.example.com
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# ── Auth ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH_MODE=demo → passwordless pick-a-user login (dev only).
# AUTH_MODE=sso  → IdP redirect/callback (see OIDC_* below); demo login disabled.
# AUTH_MODE=demo
JWT_SECRET=dev-insecure-secret-change-me
# AUTH_COOKIE_NAME=llm_platform_token
# AUTH_ISSUER=llm-platform-demo
# COOKIE_DOMAIN=        # set to .example.com so the cookie is sent to api.* and studio.*
# COOKIE_SECURE=false   # must be true in prod (HTTPS-only cookie)
# TOKEN_EXPIRY=12h

# ── SSO / OIDC (only when AUTH_MODE=sso) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Wire these to Meesho's IdP (or any OIDC provider); see auth_sso_handlers.go.
# OIDC_ISSUER=
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=https://api.example.com/auth/sso/callback
# OIDC_POST_LOGIN_URL=https://studio.example.com

# ── Prediction cache (redis if REDIS_ADDR set, else memory, else off) ──────────
# CACHE_BACKEND=memory
# REDIS_ADDR=
# REDIS_PASSWORD=
# REDIS_DB=0

# ── Per-(task, model) health breaker ───────────────────────────────────────────
# HEALTH_BREAKER_ENABLED=true
# HEALTH_FAILURE_THRESHOLD=3
# HEALTH_BASE_COOLDOWN=30s
# HEALTH_MAX_COOLDOWN=30m

# ── Per-task request/token rate limiter ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Each task gets its own rolling window with three gates:
#   1. Per-request input cap (413 if estimate exceeds MaxInputTokens)
#   2. Request-rate cap (429 if requests exceed MaxRequests per window)
#   3. Token budget (429 if tokens would exceed MaxTokens, counted upfront and
#      reconciled to actual consumption after the request, incl. failed/fallback
#      attempts). A 0 for any Max disables that particular gate.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=true               # on/off for the whole limiter
# RATE_WINDOW=1m                        # rolling window per task
# RATE_MAX_REQUESTS=600                 # max accepted requests per task per window
# RATE_MAX_TOKENS=200000                # max tokens consumed per task per window
# RATE_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=16000           # max input tokens per single request
# RATE_CHARS_PER_TOKEN=4                # estimation: ~chars per token
# RATE_TOKENS_PER_IMAGE=1000            # estimation: flat cost per attached image
